      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.89,
      "end_seconds": 3.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "hi doctor, am I too early?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 4.32,
      "end_seconds": 8.38,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "No problem at all, come in. What's troubling you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.36,
      "end_seconds": 19.0,
      "duration_seconds": 8.64,
      "text": "Mainly a heaviness in my left arm. There's a couple of other things, but that's the main one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.83,
      "end_seconds": 23.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "How many days or weeks has it been?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.92,
      "end_seconds": 28.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "It's, It's been nearly five years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.0,
      "end_seconds": 36.73,
      "duration_seconds": 7.73,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 38.38,
      "end_seconds": 53.38,
      "duration_seconds": 15.0,
      "text": "Resting helps a bit i'd call it moderate i looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help there's a tight feeling in my chest when I walk uphill as well"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 55.32,
      "end_seconds": 58.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "I'll just record a few vital signs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 64.85,
      "end_seconds": 67.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "keep your arm relaxed for me.."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 82.1,
      "end_seconds": 88.42,
      "duration_seconds": 6.32,
      "text": "okay: pulse 75, blood pressure 119 over 72, oxygen saturation is 97 percent"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.2,
      "end_seconds": 90.71,
      "duration_seconds": 1.51,
      "text": "Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.29,
      "end_seconds": 96.49,
      "duration_seconds": 4.2,
      "text": "They help me see the whole picture, more shortly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.98,
      "end_seconds": 102.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "now I'm going to do a short physical check"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.02,
      "end_seconds": 105.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "I'm just checking this side."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 124.17,
      "end_seconds": 127.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "there is no swelling in your ankles"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 129.84,
      "end_seconds": 131.68,
      "duration_seconds": 1.84,
      "text": "Please sit back down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.81,
      "end_seconds": 146.92,
      "duration_seconds": 5.11,
      "text": "any palpitations, fainting or pain between the shoulder blades at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 147.67,
      "end_seconds": 153.11,
      "duration_seconds": 5.44,
      "text": "No, no palpitations, fainting or pain between the shoulder blades."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.03,
      "end_seconds": 158.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "have you had ankle swelling, by any chance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 159.42,
      "end_seconds": 164.18,
      "duration_seconds": 4.76,
      "text": "No, you know, I haven't had any ankle swelling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.92,
      "end_seconds": 168.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "Anything different when you pass water?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 169.78,
      "end_seconds": 173.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "That's normal as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 175.53,
      "end_seconds": 179.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.32,
      "end_seconds": 184.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "Not to my knowledge, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.38,
      "end_seconds": 195.67,
      "duration_seconds": 4.29,
      "text": "Do you have any medical conditions I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.9,
      "end_seconds": 198.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "No, nothing at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.81,
      "end_seconds": 217.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "Right, do you take any regular medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 218.68,
      "end_seconds": 221.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "Nothing regular, um, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.47,
      "end_seconds": 233.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.19,
      "text": "Are you active?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 236.75,
      "end_seconds": 240.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "I walk the dog every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 240.7,
      "end_seconds": 242.26,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "How are your meals?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 243.69,
      "end_seconds": 247.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "I grab fast food at lunch most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.16,
      "end_seconds": 252.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "What do you do during the day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 252.83,
      "end_seconds": 256.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "I look after my grandchildren most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.16,
      "end_seconds": 264.07,
      "duration_seconds": 6.91,
      "text": "From what you've told me and what I found, this is probably exertional angina until proven otherwise."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 264.96,
      "end_seconds": 268.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "I'm scared it's something bad is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.9,
      "end_seconds": 284.57,
      "duration_seconds": 14.67,
      "text": "nothing I've seen today points to an emergency it looks like exertional angina until proven otherwise, but I'd like to confirm i'll request blood tests, it'll help with cardiovascular risk"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 285.88,
      "end_seconds": 288.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "How long will it take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 289.6,
      "end_seconds": 323.4,
      "duration_seconds": 33.8,
      "text": "The treatment will be GTN spray, 400 micrograms, when needed for chest pain, long term. It's for chest pain. If the tightness comes, stop, sit down and use the spray under your tongue. We'll refer you to the cardiology clinic. If the chest pain lasts more than ten minutes or comes at rest, that's the point to come in urgently. Let's plan a check in two weeks. That's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 324.99,
      "end_seconds": 327.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "thank you, doctor, goodbye"
    }
  ]
